{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg3N8mXQjwjarwWejuaSt","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[x] SSR suite: static pages stay byte-identical.\n\nThe host tag serializer now leaves out any extra (non-prop) attribute whose name isn't a valid HTML attribute name. All three checklist items are done and committed. Lint is clean, the SSR suite passes 82/82 and `npm test` passes 286/286.\n\n**Where the check lives:** The hydration DX spec's ticket 13, which moves the serializer out of core, hasn't landed yet. So the check went where the serializer lives today, `_renderHost` in `src/builders.ts`, as the ticket allows. The new `_attrName` regex (`/^[a-z_:][-\\w:.]*$/i`) matches the spec's grammar. Names that fail it are skipped without an error. Declared prop names aren't checked.\n\n**Tests, all in `test/ssr.ts`:**\n1. A render with a mix of hostile and valid extra keys, including `x\" onload=\"...\"`. Only the valid ones reach the host tag. This failed before the fix and passes after.\n2. An exact host-tag string for declared props, including a prop named `$odd`, which is outside the grammar but still serializes. It passed on the first run, as a guard against regressions should. To show it can catch a change, I made the serializer validate declared names too: the test failed, and I reverted that change.\n3. No new test. The existing exact-string test, `html SSR: static page output is unchanged`, already covers it and still passes.\n\n**Things to know:**\n- **Retry:** The first `npm test` run failed on `EADDRINUSE :8123` because another worktree was using the port. That was the only reason attempt 1 failed, and its commits were not kept, so I redid the work. A retry loop then passed on its first run.\n- **Size:** Core is 4.19 kB against its 4.2 kB limit, which I left unchanged. That leaves about 10 B, so the host-moves ticket will probably have to raise the limit.\n- **AGENTS.md:** I added a note to move `_attrName` along with `_renderHost` when ticket 13 lands, and on how little size room core has left.\n\nNotes for the orchestrator are in `.nightralph/notes.md`, which is not committed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":485,"cache_read_input_tokens":65183,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":485},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0e60305c-3d2c-4a81-8765-7059b7045ef9","uuid":"0d554dc0-c6f4-4629-bc33-9993f62b5a00","timestamp":"2026-10-15T04:08:20.847Z","request_id":"req_011Cg3N8mB4wHQaQgrGgk9wL"}
